1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,371
这是一个叫 translation-audio 的 Cloud Run job
Here is a Cloud Run job called translation-audio.

2
00:00:03,691 --> 00:00:08,277
它用的 image 和一个运行得好好的翻译 web 应用一样
It uses the same image as a translation web app that works perfectly.

3
00:00:08,597 --> 00:00:11,051
我们点 Execute，这个 job 就开始了
We press Execute, and the job starts.

4
00:00:11,733 --> 00:00:12,984
几分钟过去了
Minutes pass.

5
00:00:13,034 --> 00:00:17,365
输出 bucket 里什么也没有，这个 job 也从来不说自己完成了
Nothing lands in the output bucket, and the job never says it is done.

6
00:00:17,685 --> 00:00:20,586
它一头撞上我们设的任务超时
It runs straight into the task timeout we gave it.

7
00:00:20,906 --> 00:00:23,232
5 分钟，平台把它停掉了
5 minutes, and the platform stops it.

8
00:00:23,467 --> 00:00:26,163
线索在 Dockerfile 的最后一行
The clue is the last line of the Dockerfile:

9
00:00:26,163 --> 00:00:28,736
它的默认命令会启动 web 服务器
its default command starts the web server.

10
00:00:29,056 --> 00:00:32,792
README 的故障排查表甚至列出了这个症状
The README's troubleshooting table even lists the symptom:

11
00:00:32,792 --> 00:00:35,883
一个 job 启动了服务器，而不是跑完
a job that starts a server instead of finishing.

12
00:00:36,117 --> 00:00:37,802
同一个 image，同一份代码
Same image, same code.

13
00:00:38,122 --> 00:00:41,386
那为什么 web 应用能用，这个 job 却永远不结束？
So why does the web app work, while the job never ends?

14
00:00:41,706 --> 00:00:43,306
先记着这个问题
Hold that question.

15
00:00:44,817 --> 00:00:48,081
对这次小测来说，这一讲归结为五个考点
For the quiz, this lecture comes down to five ideas.

16
00:00:48,401 --> 00:00:50,001
是 service 还是 job
Service or job.

17
00:00:50,065 --> 00:00:51,729
谁为空闲时间付钱
Who pays for idle time.

18
00:00:52,049 --> 00:00:53,756
部署时你要交出什么
What you hand over to deploy.

19
00:00:54,076 --> 00:00:56,508
谁能调用你的代码，它又以谁的身份运行
Who may call your code, and who it runs as.

20
00:00:56,828 --> 00:01:01,414
还有模型 endpoint：预处理放在哪里，它调用哪个函数
And the model endpoint: where preprocessing lives, and which function it calls.

21
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:06,109
右上角的灰色标签，标出每个考点背后的那页课件
The gray tag, top right, names the lecture slide behind each idea.

22
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:13,442
课上说，Cloud Run 可以把一个 container
The lecture says Cloud Run runs a container

23
00:01:13,442 --> 00:01:15,042
作为 service 或 job 来运行
as a service or a job.

24
00:01:15,293 --> 00:01:16,900
这个演示应用两种都有
The demo app shows both:

25
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:20,114
一个 image，两个启动命令，serve 或 batch
one image, two startup commands, serve or batch.

26
00:01:20,350 --> 00:01:23,047
这个 serve 命令启动 gunicorn，一个 web 服务器
Serve starts gunicorn, a web server,

27
00:01:23,047 --> 00:01:26,643
跑在 Cloud Run 给它的 port 上，默认是 8080
on the port Cloud Run gives it, 8080 by default.

28
00:01:26,963 --> 00:01:30,057
然后它就等着，来一个请求就回答一个
Then it waits, and answers each request that arrives.

29
00:01:30,650 --> 00:01:32,250
这种形状就是 service
That shape is a service.

30
00:01:32,485 --> 00:01:38,693
它有 URL，流量上来时加实例，流量停了可以缩容到零
It has a URL, adds instances when traffic rises, and can scale to zero when it stops.

31
00:01:39,013 --> 00:01:42,362
它本来就不会结束：监听就是它的本职工作
It never finishes on purpose: listening is its job.

32
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:44,200
而 batch 是另一种形状
Batch has a different shape.

33
00:01:44,413 --> 00:01:49,875
它读入那段文字，翻译它，生成语音，保存文件，然后退出
It reads the passage, translates it, generates speech, saves the files, and exits.

34
00:01:50,195 --> 00:01:52,924
如果某一步失败，它以退出码 1 退出
If a step fails, it exits with status 1,

35
00:01:52,924 --> 00:01:56,403
所以这次执行显示失败，而不是假的成功
so the execution shows failed, not a false success.

36
00:01:56,650 --> 00:02:01,450
README 把这叫做 job：没有 URL，没有东西在等请求
The README calls this a job: no URL, nothing waiting for requests.

37
00:02:01,770 --> 00:02:04,501
有东西启动它，它就一直跑到完成
Something starts it, and it runs to completion.

38
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:06,023
现在回到开头
Now the hook.

39
00:02:06,073 --> 00:02:09,550
这个 job 继承了 image 的默认命令，也就是 serve
The job inherited the image's default command, serve,

40
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:13,945
所以它启动了 web 服务器，等着永远不会来的请求
so it started a web server and waited for requests that never come.

41
00:02:14,265 --> 00:02:17,401
修复：命令用 python，再加上 batch 参数
The fix: the command python, with the batch arguments.

42
00:02:17,721 --> 00:02:20,067
同一个 image，现在时间条有了尽头
Same image, and now the strip ends.

43
00:02:20,317 --> 00:02:21,824
谁来按开始？
Who presses start?

44
00:02:21,874 --> 00:02:24,050
在 README 里，是你点 Execute
In the README, you click Execute.

45
00:02:24,370 --> 00:02:27,940
如果要每晚运行，常用的触发器是 Cloud Scheduler
For a nightly run, the usual trigger is Cloud Scheduler,

46
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:29,917
不过这个 README 没有用它
which this README does not use.

47
00:02:30,617 --> 00:02:31,847
来试一道
Try one.

48
00:02:31,897 --> 00:02:35,780
一个 container 给新文档建索引，然后退出，每小时一次
A container indexes new documents and exits, once an hour.

49
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:38,595
看生命周期，别看产品名
Read the lifecycle, not the product names.

50
00:02:49,933 --> 00:02:52,942
选 B，按 Cloud Scheduler 时间表运行的 job
B, a job on a Cloud Scheduler timetable:

51
00:02:52,942 --> 00:02:56,930
它跑到完成，两次运行之间不花钱
it runs to completion and costs nothing between runs.

52
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:59,441
A 整个小时都在为一个实例付钱
A pays for an instance all hour,

53
00:02:59,441 --> 00:03:03,480
而且空闲的 service 的 CPU 会被节流，所以循环会卡住
and an idle service's CPU is throttled, so the loop stalls.

54
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:07,960
C 违反了 service 的约定：一个退出了的实例就是崩溃了
C breaks the service contract: an instance that exits has crashed.

55
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:11,928
D 能用，但这台 VM 整个小时都要付钱，哪怕它闲着
D works, but the VM is paid for all hour while it idles.

56
00:03:12,248 --> 00:03:13,891
为什么这很重要，下面就讲
Why that matters is next.

57
00:03:14,133 --> 00:03:18,800
所以规则是：如果题目说它运行、写出结果然后退出
So the rule: if the question says it runs, writes its output and exits,

58
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:21,429
或者说它每晚运行，选 job
or that it runs every night, pick a job.

59
00:03:21,749 --> 00:03:24,596
如果题目说它回答请求、有 URL
If it says it answers requests, has a URL,

60
00:03:24,596 --> 00:03:27,104
或者监听一个 port，选 service
or listens on a port, pick a service.

61
00:03:32,383 --> 00:03:35,562
课上承诺，只有代码运行时你才付钱
The lecture promises you pay only while your code runs.

62
00:03:35,882 --> 00:03:38,698
我们把它说准确：两个计价器，一天
Let's make that exact: two meters, one day.

63
00:03:39,018 --> 00:03:40,767
黄色刻度是请求
The yellow ticks are requests.

64
00:03:41,016 --> 00:03:43,128
上面一行是一台虚拟机
The top row is a virtual machine.

65
00:03:43,448 --> 00:03:47,032
它的计价器从开机走到关机，不管有没有请求
Its meter runs from boot to shutdown, requests or not.

66
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:50,894
金色阴影是空闲时间，这些你全部都要付钱
The gold shading is idle time, and you pay for all of it.

67
00:03:51,133 --> 00:03:53,165
下面一行是一个函数
The bottom row is a function,

68
00:03:53,165 --> 00:03:58,089
或者一个按请求计费、最小实例数为 0 的 Cloud Run service
or a Cloud Run service with request-based billing and minimum instances 0,

69
00:03:58,089 --> 00:03:59,689
和 README 里一样
as in the README.

70
00:03:59,858 --> 00:04:04,040
它的计价器只随调用次数和每次运行多长时间而动
Its meter moves only with invocations and how long each one runs.

71
00:04:04,450 --> 00:04:07,138
现在把请求之间的安静间隔拉长
Now stretch the quiet gaps between requests.

72
00:04:07,458 --> 00:04:12,002
VM 的计价器往上涨，因为空闲的小时仍然是预配的小时
The VM meter grows, because idle hours are still provisioned hours.

73
00:04:12,322 --> 00:04:16,482
函数的计价器完全不动：没有请求，就没有费用
The function meter does not move at all: no requests, no charge.

74
00:04:16,716 --> 00:04:21,879
零空闲成本是有代价的，课件第 16 页点出了它：冷启动
Zero idle cost has a price, and slide 16 names it: the cold start.

75
00:04:22,199 --> 00:04:26,273
安静一阵之后，第一个请求要等一个实例启动
After a quiet stretch, the first request waits while an instance starts.

76
00:04:26,593 --> 00:04:29,367
README 的办法是最小实例数
The README's remedy is minimum instances.

77
00:04:29,687 --> 00:04:33,753
把它设成 1，就有一个热实例一直开着等第一个请求
Set it to 1, and a warm instance stays on for the first request,

78
00:04:33,753 --> 00:04:35,468
它自己的计价器也在走
with its own meter running.

79
00:04:35,716 --> 00:04:38,959
这个常驻实例现在就落在 VM 那一行
That always-on instance now sits in the VM row.

80
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:42,237
下一讲的 Vertex AI endpoint 也一样
So does next lecture's Vertex AI endpoint:

81
00:04:42,237 --> 00:04:49,562
它的部署调用要求最小副本数为 1，README 说这就是花钱的部分
its deploy call asks for a minimum replica count of 1, which the README calls the part that costs money.

82
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,400
换个新情况试试
Test it on a new case.

83
00:04:51,613 --> 00:04:55,453
请求数翻倍，每个一样长，天数不变
Twice as many requests, each just as long, in the same days.

84
00:04:55,773 --> 00:04:57,373
哪份账单会变？
Which bill changes?

85
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,600
选 B，只有函数的
B, only the function's.

86
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:14,133
看：每个请求一分为二，函数的计价器往上涨
Watch: every request splits in two, and the function meter climbs,

87
00:05:14,133 --> 00:05:17,643
因为每次调用和它的运行时间都要计费
since every invocation and its running time are billed.

88
00:05:17,963 --> 00:05:24,405
VM 的计价器不动，因为它按预配的时长计费：A 说反了，C 是错的
The VM meter does not move, because it bills provisioned hours: A is backwards, and C is wrong.

89
00:05:24,725 --> 00:05:27,861
D 把没有最低收费和免费干活混为一谈
D confuses no minimum charge with free work.

90
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:30,511
所以规则不是：serverless 很便宜
So the rule is not, serverless is cheap.

91
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:33,284
规则是：有没有什么东西一直开着？
The rule is: is anything always on?

92
00:05:33,604 --> 00:05:37,124
空闲时间只影响常驻资源的账单
Idle time moves only the bills of always-on things.

93
00:05:37,444 --> 00:05:41,241
请求数和时长只影响按用量计费的账单
Request count and duration move only the pay-per-use bill.

94
00:05:45,983 --> 00:05:47,732
接下来，你要交出什么
Next, what you hand over.

95
00:05:48,052 --> 00:05:51,426
课上用四种方式部署同一个翻译应用
The lecture deploys one translate app four ways:

96
00:05:51,426 --> 00:05:55,220
虚拟机或 serverless，代码文件或 container
virtual machine or serverless, code file or container.

97
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:57,951
前面几讲填好了 VM 那一行
Earlier lectures filled the VM row.

98
00:05:58,271 --> 00:06:00,276
今天填 serverless 那一行
Today fills the serverless row.

99
00:06:00,516 --> 00:06:03,140
部署函数，你交出一个源文件
For a function you hand over a source file,

100
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:05,337
它的 requirements 文件，再加一个名字
its requirements file, and one name.

101
00:06:05,657 --> 00:06:07,453
这个文件是 main.py
The file is main.py:

102
00:06:07,453 --> 00:06:10,506
一个叫 hello 下划线 http 的 HTTP 处理函数
an HTTP handler called hello_http,

103
00:06:10,506 --> 00:06:15,983
它从请求里读出文本和两个语言代码
which reads the text and two language codes from the request.

104
00:06:16,233 --> 00:06:20,542
这个名字就是入口点：框架应该调用的那个 Python 函数
That name is the entry point: the Python function the framework should call.

105
00:06:20,862 --> 00:06:23,486
不是文件名，也不是 service 名称
Not the file name, and not the service name.

106
00:06:23,733 --> 00:06:25,304
然后由 Google 构建
Then Google builds.

107
00:06:25,354 --> 00:06:30,345
Cloud Build 安装依赖，配置 Functions Framework
Cloud Build installs the requirements, configures the Functions Framework,

108
00:06:30,345 --> 00:06:33,312
再把一个 image 发布到 Artifact Registry
and publishes an image to Artifact Registry.

109
00:06:33,632 --> 00:06:37,216
这只在构建时发生一次，不是每个请求都来一次
This happens once, at build time, not on every request.

110
00:06:37,450 --> 00:06:39,989
框架靠这个名字找到你的函数
The framework finds your function by that name.

111
00:06:40,309 --> 00:06:44,383
入口点填 main，就找不到任何叫 main 的东西
Type main as the entry point, and there is nothing called main to find.

112
00:06:44,703 --> 00:06:48,159
函数构建失败，构建日志会告诉你原因
The function build fails, and its build logs tell you why.

113
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:52,624
课件第 11 页说，运行函数不用管理 container
Slide 11 says a function runs without managing containers.

114
00:06:52,944 --> 00:06:55,973
你不用管理它，但 Google 照样会构建一个
You do not manage one, but Google still builds one.

115
00:06:56,293 --> 00:06:59,984
课件里的 Cloud Functions 现在叫 Cloud Run functions
And the slides' Cloud Functions are now Cloud Run functions.

116
00:07:00,233 --> 00:07:01,893
部署 Cloud Run service
For a Cloud Run service,

117
00:07:01,893 --> 00:07:04,798
你交出一个现成的 image，给出它的 URL
you hand over a finished image by its URL.

118
00:07:05,118 --> 00:07:08,852
部署它什么也不构建：这个 image 事先就构建好了
Deploying it builds nothing: the image was built beforehand.

119
00:07:09,172 --> 00:07:13,244
它的 Dockerfile 选定了基础 Python、默认 port 8080
Its Dockerfile picks the base Python, the default port, 8080,

120
00:07:13,244 --> 00:07:14,846
以及启动命令
and the startup command.

121
00:07:15,166 --> 00:07:16,766
这三样都由你控制
You control all three.

122
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:19,844
两者都通过 HTTPS URL 调用
Both are called through an HTTPS URL.

123
00:07:20,164 --> 00:07:24,516
函数通过查询字符串接收新的输入，不用重新部署
The function takes new inputs through its query string, with no redeploy.

124
00:07:25,950 --> 00:07:30,323
两者最后都是同一样东西：Cloud Run 上的一个 container 实例
Both end as the same thing: a container instance on Cloud Run.

125
00:07:30,643 --> 00:07:33,331
函数就是一个不用你自己写的 container
A function is a container you did not write.

126
00:07:33,651 --> 00:07:36,873
在小测上，源代码加入口点，就是函数
On the quiz, source plus an entry point means a function.

127
00:07:37,193 --> 00:07:40,904
你自己的 image，或者你自己的启动命令，就是 service
Your own image, or your own startup command, means a service.

128
00:07:46,150 --> 00:07:49,244
每个部署好的 service 都面对两个权限问题
Every deployed service faces two permission questions,

129
00:07:49,244 --> 00:07:51,249
README 把它们分开处理
and the README keeps them separate.

130
00:07:51,569 --> 00:07:53,169
谁能调用我们的公开应用？
Who may call our public app?

131
00:07:53,446 --> 00:07:55,387
运行中的应用又能访问什么？
And what may the running app access?

132
00:07:55,633 --> 00:07:57,254
左边的门是调用方
The left door is the caller.

133
00:07:57,574 --> 00:08:01,308
允许公开访问时，任何浏览器的请求都能进来
With public access allowed, any browser's request gets in.

134
00:08:01,628 --> 00:08:06,034
不允许的话，没有权限的调用方会被 403 挡回去
Without it, a caller with no permission is turned away with a 403,

135
00:08:06,034 --> 00:08:07,836
你的代码根本不会运行
before your code even runs.

136
00:08:08,083 --> 00:08:10,920
右边的门是你的代码向外调用时的身份
The right door is who your code is when it calls out.

137
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:14,204
这个 web 应用戴着服务账号工牌
The web app wears a service account badge,

138
00:08:14,204 --> 00:08:17,097
translation-demo-runtime，有两个角色
translation-demo-runtime, with two roles:

139
00:08:17,097 --> 00:08:20,414
Agent Platform User 和 Service Usage Consumer
Agent Platform User and Service Usage Consumer.

140
00:08:20,734 --> 00:08:22,910
你不用创建或下载密钥
You do not create or download a key.

141
00:08:23,150 --> 00:08:25,838
代码只是请求默认凭据
The code just asks for default credentials,

142
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:30,339
而在 Cloud Run 上平台会把所挂账号的 token 交给它
and on Cloud Run the platform hands it a token for the attached account.

143
00:08:30,659 --> 00:08:32,259
哪里都没有密钥文件
No key file anywhere.

144
00:08:32,467 --> 00:08:34,067
还有一个箭头，来自你
One more arrow, from you.

145
00:08:34,323 --> 00:08:36,491
要把这个工牌挂到一个 service 上
To attach that badge to a service,

146
00:08:36,491 --> 00:08:39,742
你自己的身份需要这个账号的 Service Account User 角色
your own identity needs Service Account User on it.

147
00:08:40,062 --> 00:08:44,413
这是部署权限，和工牌本身能做什么是两回事
That is a deployment permission, separate from what the badge itself may do.

148
00:08:44,650 --> 00:08:46,442
这个 job 有自己的工牌
The job gets its own badge.

149
00:08:46,762 --> 00:08:49,503
它有同样的两个 Agent Platform 角色
It has the same two Agent Platform roles,

150
00:08:49,503 --> 00:08:52,577
另外在输入 bucket 上有 Storage Object Viewer
plus Storage Object Viewer on the input bucket

151
00:08:52,577 --> 00:08:55,786
在输出 bucket 上有 Storage Object Creator
and Storage Object Creator on the output bucket.

152
00:08:56,106 --> 00:08:58,757
这个 web 应用的账号不需要任何 bucket 角色
The web app's account needs no bucket roles,

153
00:08:58,757 --> 00:09:01,589
因为它的音频直接发给浏览器
because its audio goes straight to the browser.

154
00:09:01,909 --> 00:09:03,509
一个工作负载一个工牌
One badge per workload.

155
00:09:03,733 --> 00:09:07,360
课件第 16 页提醒，serverless 更难调试
Slide 16 warns that serverless is harder to debug.

156
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:12,305
README 说了去哪看：函数构建失败看构建日志
The README says where to look: build logs when a function build fails,

157
00:09:12,305 --> 00:09:16,533
请求失败看 service 日志，还有 job 的执行日志
service logs when a request fails, and the job's execution logs.

158
00:09:16,853 --> 00:09:19,243
构建成功不代表它能用
A finished build is not proof that it works.

159
00:09:19,483 --> 00:09:22,392
规则是：公开访问回答谁能调用
The rule: public access answers who may call,

160
00:09:22,392 --> 00:09:25,883
被拒绝的调用方在你的代码运行之前就被挡住了
and a refused caller is stopped before your code runs.

161
00:09:26,203 --> 00:09:29,190
服务账号回答你的代码能碰什么
The service account answers what your code may touch.

162
00:09:29,510 --> 00:09:33,393
当你自己的代码被拒绝时，修的是工牌的角色，不是调用方
When your own code is denied, fix the badge's roles, not the caller.

163
00:09:38,433 --> 00:09:42,945
要部署一个训练好的模型，下一讲用的是 Vertex AI endpoint
To serve a trained model, the next lecture uses a Vertex AI endpoint,

164
00:09:42,945 --> 00:09:46,476
小测问的是它的预处理应该放在哪里
and the quiz asks where its preprocessing should live.

165
00:09:46,796 --> 00:09:49,825
想象两个客户端：一个手机应用，一个网页
Picture two clients: a phone app, and a web page.

166
00:09:50,066 --> 00:09:53,324
每个客户端都带着同一个齿轮
Each client carries the same gear:

167
00:09:53,324 --> 00:09:58,402
解码 JPEG，把像素缩放到 0 到 1 之间
decode the JPEG, scale the pixels to between 0 and 1,

168
00:09:58,402 --> 00:10:00,797
再 resize 到 224 乘 224
and resize to 224 by 224.

169
00:10:01,117 --> 00:10:03,719
然后它才把数字发给模型
Only then does it send numbers to the model.

170
00:10:04,039 --> 00:10:07,560
这是同一份配方的两个副本，在两个代码库里
That is two copies of one recipe, in two code bases.

171
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:10,360
课上把这叫做客户端的脆弱性
The lecture calls this client-side brittleness.

172
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:13,660
每个客户端的预处理都略有不同
Every client preprocesses slightly differently,

173
00:10:13,660 --> 00:10:17,400
用一份配方训练的模型，悄悄收到了另一份
and a model trained on one recipe quietly receives another.

174
00:10:17,716 --> 00:10:19,721
现在把齿轮挪进 endpoint
Now move the gear into the endpoint.

175
00:10:20,041 --> 00:10:22,229
客户端发送原始的 JPEG 字节
Clients send raw JPEG bytes,

176
00:10:22,229 --> 00:10:26,527
用 base64 包起来，因为 JSON 装不了原始字节
wrapped as base64, because JSON cannot carry raw bytes.

177
00:10:26,847 --> 00:10:30,690
预处理跟着模型走，所以每个客户端得到的
The preprocessing travels with the model, so every client gets

178
00:10:30,690 --> 00:10:33,354
正好是训练时用的预处理
exactly the preprocessing used in training.

179
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:35,413
看这个 repo 自己的客户端
Look at the repo's own client.

180
00:10:35,733 --> 00:10:40,299
它读入图片文件，做 base64 编码，然后调用 predict
It reads the image files, base64 encodes them, and calls predict.

181
00:10:40,619 --> 00:10:42,965
不 resize，不归一化
No resizing, no normalizing.

182
00:10:43,285 --> 00:10:44,885
这就是瘦客户端
That is a thin client.

183
00:10:45,016 --> 00:10:47,427
现在在版本 2 里发布一个有问题的 resize
Now ship a bad resize in version 2.

184
00:10:47,747 --> 00:10:49,453
两个客户端同时坏掉
Both clients break at once.

185
00:10:49,773 --> 00:10:53,827
回滚到版本 1，两个客户端在同一瞬间恢复正常
Roll back to version 1, and both are healthy at the same instant.

186
00:10:54,147 --> 00:10:57,539
一次部署修好了所有人，不用发布任何客户端
One deployment fixed everyone, with no client release.

187
00:10:57,783 --> 00:10:59,916
现在把齿轮放回客户端
Now put the gears back on the clients.

188
00:11:00,236 --> 00:11:02,028
同样的回滚要付出什么代价？
What does the same rollback cost?

189
00:11:08,866 --> 00:11:13,965
两次发布：一个等着应用商店审核的手机更新，再加一次网页部署
Two releases: a phone update waiting in app store review, and a web deploy.

190
00:11:14,285 --> 00:11:18,253
它们上线的时间不同，在这中间，两个客户端的结果不一致
They land at different times, and in between, the clients disagree.

191
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:23,876
规则是：当题目说有好几个客户端，要在一个地方更新或回滚
The rule: when the question says several clients, one place to update or roll back,

192
00:11:23,876 --> 00:11:27,567
而且不用发布客户端时，把预处理放在 endpoint
and no client release, put preprocessing at the endpoint.

193
00:11:27,887 --> 00:11:32,686
预处理放在客户端，就意味着每个客户端都要同步重新发布
Preprocessing on the clients means every client is re-released in lockstep.

194
00:11:37,633 --> 00:11:39,405
把预处理放在 endpoint
Preprocessing at the endpoint

195
00:11:39,405 --> 00:11:42,582
只有在 endpoint 调用了正确的函数时才有用
works only if the endpoint calls the right function.

196
00:11:42,902 --> 00:11:47,231
这条链是：JPEG 字节，解码，转成浮点数，resize
Here is the chain: JPEG bytes, decode, convert to floats, resize,

197
00:11:47,231 --> 00:11:50,561
模型，最后是四个概率，每种奶酪一个
the model, and four probabilities, one per cheese.

198
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:55,280
在这个 repo 里，preprocess image 做前三步，一次处理一张图
In the repo, preprocess_image does the first three steps, for one image.

199
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:57,882
它返回的是一张图片，不是答案
It returns an image, not an answer.

200
00:11:58,116 --> 00:12:00,947
这个 serving function 接收一批字符串
The serving_function takes a batch of strings,

201
00:12:00,947 --> 00:12:04,516
对每一个都套用 preprocess image，然后调用模型
maps preprocess_image over each one, then calls the model.

202
00:12:04,836 --> 00:12:07,631
预处理和推理，在同一个函数里
Preprocessing and inference, in one function.

203
00:12:07,951 --> 00:12:11,257
它的参数 bytes inputs，就是客户端要用的键
Its argument, bytes_inputs, is the key clients use.

204
00:12:11,577 --> 00:12:14,453
考题可能把这个函数叫做 serve
Exam questions may call this function serve:

205
00:12:14,453 --> 00:12:19,876
不是 web 应用的 serve 命令，而是先预处理、再预测的那个函数
not the web app's serve command, but the function that preprocesses, then predicts.

206
00:12:20,116 --> 00:12:23,377
导出时把它注册在 serving default 这个名字下面
The export registers it under the name serving_default,

207
00:12:23,377 --> 00:12:26,815
模型服务器调用的就是这个名字背后的东西
and the model server calls whatever sits behind that name.

208
00:12:27,135 --> 00:12:30,954
课件用另一种调用来保存它；道理是一样的
The slide saves it with a different call; the idea is the same.

209
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:33,547
试插头之前，最后检查一次
Before we try plugs, one last check.

210
00:12:33,867 --> 00:12:38,346
一个手机应用发送浮点数组，一个新的网页客户端发送 JPEG 字节
A phone app sends float arrays, a new web client sends JPEG bytes,

211
00:12:38,346 --> 00:12:41,739
团队想只在一个地方修预处理
and the team wants one place to fix preprocessing.

212
00:12:42,059 --> 00:12:43,659
他们应该注册什么？
What should they register?

213
00:12:56,366 --> 00:12:59,801
先试 B：只注册 preprocess image
Try B first: register preprocess_image alone.

214
00:13:00,121 --> 00:13:05,241
请求返回的是一张 224 乘 224 的图片
A request comes back as a 224 by 224 image.

215
00:13:05,561 --> 00:13:07,161
根本没有做分类
Nothing was classified.

216
00:13:07,316 --> 00:13:09,065
A 和 D 保留原始模型
A and D keep the raw model.

217
00:13:09,385 --> 00:13:13,311
它要的是浮点张量，所以 JPEG 字节插不进去
It demands float tensors, so JPEG bytes no longer fit.

218
00:13:13,631 --> 00:13:16,852
服务器只会把 base64 变回字节
The server only turns base64 back into bytes.

219
00:13:17,172 --> 00:13:21,418
齿轮又跳回了每个客户端：两个副本要保持同步
The gears jump back onto every client: two copies to keep in sync.

220
00:13:21,666 --> 00:13:25,741
选 C，serving function：字节进去，概率出来
C, the serving_function: bytes go in, probabilities come out.

221
00:13:26,061 --> 00:13:29,133
手机应用改成发送字节，只需一次
The phone app switches to sending bytes once;

222
00:13:29,133 --> 00:13:35,618
之后，一个导出的版本就装着配方，每次修复或回滚都是一次部署
after that, one exported version holds the recipe, and every fix or rollback is one deployment.

223
00:13:35,938 --> 00:13:38,657
这个 repo 的测试步骤加载 serving default
The repo's test step loads serving_default

224
00:13:38,657 --> 00:13:41,634
喂给它 bytes inputs，和服务器的做法一样
and feeds it bytes_inputs, as the server will.

225
00:13:41,883 --> 00:13:44,385
这和函数的入口点是同一个道理
This echoes the function's entry point:

226
00:13:44,385 --> 00:13:50,480
平台只调用你注册的那个名字，名字错了，下游什么也补救不了
the platform calls exactly the name you registered, and nothing downstream can fix a wrong one.

227
00:13:50,716 --> 00:13:55,025
规则是：注册那个做预处理和推理的函数
The rule: register the function that does preprocessing and inference.

228
00:13:55,345 --> 00:14:01,106
单独的预处理返回的是图片，原始模型会让每个客户端自己预处理
Preprocessing alone returns images, and the raw model makes every client preprocess.

229
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:07,171
周二的七条规则
Seven rules for Tuesday.

230
00:14:07,491 --> 00:14:09,219
第一：看生命周期
One: read the lifecycle.

231
00:14:09,539 --> 00:14:11,825
如果它在监听，它就是 service
If it listens, it is a service;

232
00:14:11,825 --> 00:14:14,333
如果它运行完就退出，它就是 job
if it runs and exits, it is a job,

233
00:14:14,333 --> 00:14:17,283
按需启动或者由 Cloud Scheduler 启动
started on demand or by Cloud Scheduler.

234
00:14:17,603 --> 00:14:20,697
第二：空闲时间只让一直开着的东西花钱
Two: idle time costs only what is always on.

235
00:14:21,017 --> 00:14:25,161
第三：按用量计费，计的是调用次数和执行时间
Three: pay-per-use bills invocations and execution time,

236
00:14:25,161 --> 00:14:28,121
零空闲成本换来的是冷启动
and zero idle cost buys you cold starts.

237
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:34,176
第四：函数是源代码、依赖和入口点，image 由 Google 构建
Four: a function is source, requirements and an entry point, and Google builds the image;

238
00:14:34,176 --> 00:14:36,004
service 是你自己的 image
a service is your own image.

239
00:14:36,324 --> 00:14:39,161
第五：谁能调用它，不等于它以谁的身份运行
Five: who may call it is not who it runs as,

240
00:14:39,161 --> 00:14:42,063
运行时的服务账号也不需要密钥
and the runtime service account needs no key.

241
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:44,509
第六：在 endpoint 做预处理
Six: preprocess at the endpoint,

242
00:14:44,509 --> 00:14:48,167
这样一次部署就能更新或回滚每个客户端
so one deployment updates or rolls back every client.

243
00:14:48,487 --> 00:14:53,570
第七：注册先预处理、再调用模型的 serving function
Seven: register the serving function that preprocesses and then calls the model,

244
00:14:53,570 --> 00:14:57,191
因为平台只调用你注册的那个名字
because the platform calls exactly the name you register.

245
00:14:57,433 --> 00:14:58,940
该用哪一个？
Which one to use?

246
00:14:58,990 --> 00:15:04,608
下一讲的经验法则：Vertex AI 用来在生产环境部署训练好的模型
The next lecture's rule of thumb: Vertex AI to serve a trained model in production,

247
00:15:04,608 --> 00:15:07,993
Cloud Run 用在模型只是更大应用一部分的时候
Cloud Run when the model is part of a broader app.

248
00:15:08,313 --> 00:15:14,052
还要记住课件第 16 页说的代价：厂商锁定、冷启动、更难调试
And remember the costs on slide 16: vendor lock-in, cold starts, harder debugging.

249
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:16,305
这就是这一讲的七条规则
That's the lecture in seven rules.

250
00:15:16,625 --> 00:15:18,225
周二小测加油
Good luck on Tuesday.
